Coordinate chemical production and distribution without losing process feasibility (@cs-production-planning: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Enterprise-wide-Optimization-Grossmann.lingua#r_4XD1X5QN83H40RBMGJVSZY9Y8V", #source "../sources/Process-Industry-Supply-Chain-Management-Liu.lingua#r_5W74Q34MKEJAWVS30JV4QH01YQ", #source "../sources/Graduate-Supply-Chain-Planning-MIT.lingua#r_16MZ0PJM4KC10A3D9AYYESBT6P", #chemical-supply-systems "Orders-consumption-visibility-and-feedback-across-parties.lingua#r_7Q48XAW5X86H5DGJ3QW9XV6CAR") { r_6PQ79DBR4J7WBVMCB30J1HN4C9
**Read:** [Enterprise-wide Optimization: A New Frontier in Process Systems Engineering — Grossmann](../sources/Enterprise-wide-Optimization-Grossmann.lingua#r_4XD1X5QN83H40RBMGJVSZY9Y8V), the entire paper and primary model references selected for the case; [Supply chain management for the process industry — Songsong Liu](../sources/Process-Industry-Supply-Chain-Management-Liu.lingua#r_5W74Q34MKEJAWVS30JV4QH01YQ), complete planning/scheduling and integrated-production chapters; [Graduate Supply Chain Planning — MIT 15.762J](../sources/Graduate-Supply-Chain-Planning-MIT.lingua#r_16MZ0PJM4KC10A3D9AYYESBT6P), the full published coordination/optimisation assignments.

Connect a user's delivery requirements to batch campaigns, continuous production, co-products, shared equipment and changeovers. A planning model that treats every product as an independent instantaneous supply can propose a schedule the plant cannot execute. Include the time needed for cleaning, grade change, analysis and release where it matters.

Read the whole Grossmann paper and the relevant complete chapters of Liu's thesis. Reconstruct a small multiproduct example using material balances, capacity, state and sequence-dependent time. State exactly which decisions are continuous, integer or logical and which constraints represent demonstrated physical limits.

Compare a short-term feasible schedule with a longer-term inventory/distribution plan. A large order can change campaign timing upstream; co-product demand can constrain available output; and a customer's inability to receive can obstruct a planned dispatch. Investigate how information and decision horizons are coordinated. Solve a transparent small case independently before adopting a solver for a larger study. Later chemical/process engineering and operations-research subjects deepen the algorithms; this pathway requires the correct interface between produced, released, transported and usable quantities.

**Continue:** [Explain how replenishment decisions change the information seen upstream](Orders-consumption-visibility-and-feedback-across-parties.lingua#r_7Q48XAW5X86H5DGJ3QW9XV6CAR).

